  "permutation_power_limit": "With 3 seeds a paired sign-flip permutation test has only 2^3 = 8 arrangements, so its smallest attainable two-sided p is 2/8 = 0.25. NO contrast can reach p < 0.05 at this seed count regardless of effect size, and Holm only raises it further. The permutation p and its Holm adjustment are therefore reported as supplementary and MUST NOT be read as 'no significant difference'. The preregistered BCa95 CI on the seed-level paired difference carries the inference; a CI excluding zero with n=3 is weak but real evidence.",
  "primary_note": "Preregistered primaries were min_relative_distance_m and capture_rate. The bulk export provides capture_rate unconditioned, but the closest-approach aggregate is exported ONLY as closest_nocrash_mean_m (conditioned on no crash). That deviation is reported, not hidden: capture_rate carries the unconditioned primary, and the distance primary is reported in its crash-conditioned form."
 },
